          "title": "Asking for and Paying the Bill",
          "weight": 7,
          "content": [
            {
              "order": 1,
              "type": "text",
              "content": "{\"time\":1700000407000,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"vW8xY9zA0b\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"At the end of your meal, you need to pay. Here is the vocabulary and phrases you need:\"}},{\"id\":\"cD1eF2gH3i\",\"type\":\"list\",\"data\":{\"style\":\"unordered\",\"items\":[\"<b>bill</b> (British) / <b>check</b> (American) — the document showing what you owe\",\"<b>tip</b> — extra money you give the waiter for good service\",\"<b>service charge</b> — a percentage added to the bill for service\",\"<b>split the bill</b> — each person pays their own share\",\"<b>go Dutch</b> — another way to say split the bill\",\"<b>treat someone</b> — pay for another person's meal\"]}},{\"id\":\"jK4lM5nO6p\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Asking for the bill:</b><br><em>Could we have the bill, please? / Can I have the check, please? / We'd like to pay now.</em>\"}},{\"id\":\"qR7sT8uV9w\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Paying:</b><br><em>Can we pay by card? / I'll pay in cash. / Shall we split the bill? / It's my treat!</em>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.4\"}"
            },
